DG10, DG11), matching the declaration for both procedure arms.\",\"Selected report demonstration: the report demonstrates the ABSENCE of the repeated-measures-as-independent issue. It explicitly states the 48 records are repeated measurements nested within 12 vessels, tabulates one collapsed mean per digester (12 rows, each with 4 sessions), and runs the Mann-Whitney U test on the 12 vessel-level means (n = 6 vs 6), so each independent unit enters the row-independent procedure exactly once.\",\"Numerical verification supports the demonstration: recomputed vessel means match the table (e.g., DG01 = (268.3+251.1+271.4+258.4)/4 = 262.3), control/thermal means of digester means are 257.17 and 301.15, medians 258.75 and 301.30 (gap 42.55), and complete separation of the 6-vs-6 vessel means yields U = 36.0 with exact two-sided p = 2/924 = 0.002165, exactly as reported. These statistics are only reachable from 12 vessel-level values, not 48 pooled session rows (which would give U up to 576).\",\"Lock check: a lock is minted (dependence_method_authorization_v1) and its authorization follows from the declaration alone. authorized_key_columns is exactly [\\\"digester_id\\\"], identical to the declared independent-unit column with no additions or substitutions; the procedure record resolves to scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu, the row-independent procedure actually used on the per-unit values; authority_state is authorized by a human actor and the stated authority limitations correctly disclaim execution or correctness guarantees.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["Declaration check: the declared independent-unit column digester_id is consistent with the frozen data. data/input.csv contains exactly 12 distinct digester_id values (DG01-DG12), each appearing exactly 4 times (run days 6, 10, 14, 18), and pretreatment is constant within every digester_id, giving 6 vessels in the control arm (DG01, DG03, DG05, DG08, DG09, DG12) and 6 in the thermal arm (DG02, DG04, DG06, DG07, DG10, DG11), matching the declaration for both procedure arms.","Selected report demonstration: the report demonstrates the ABSENCE of the repeated-measures-as-independent issue. It explicitly states the 48 records are repeated measurements nested within 12 vessels, tabulates one collapsed mean per digester (12 rows, each with 4 sessions), and runs the Mann-Whitney U test on the 12 vessel-level means (n = 6 vs 6), so each independent unit enters the row-independent procedure exactly once.","Numerical verification supports the demonstration: recomputed vessel means match the table (e.g., DG01 = (268.3+251.1+271.4+258.4)/4 = 262.3), control/thermal means of digester means are 257.17 and 301.15, medians 258.75 and 301.30 (gap 42.55), and complete separation of the 6-vs-6 vessel means yields U = 36.0 with exact two-sided p = 2/924 = 0.002165, exactly as reported. These statistics are only reachable from 12 vessel-level values, not 48 pooled session rows (which would give U up to 576).","Lock check: a lock is minted (dependence_method_authorization_v1) and its authorization follows from the declaration alone. authorized_key_columns is exactly [\"digester_id\"], identical to the declared independent-unit column with no additions or substitutions; the procedure record resolves to scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu, the row-independent procedure actually used on the per-unit values; authority_state is authorized by a human actor and the stated authority limitations correctly disclaim execution or correctness guarantees."]},"ttft_ms":11992,"ttft_stream_ms":1779,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":20681,"uuid":"a2973967-d256-4572-973b-86efd6969e99"}
